  <Document>
    <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg/m^3), logarithmic (base-10) scale: <b>LOWEST 0.079</b> (dark blue) → common 1.41 (green/yellow) → <b>HIGHEST+ 99.93</b> (deep purple). Equal color per decade of concentration (ocean-color standard); displayed values are true concentrations, never altered. High values indicate biomass/activity, not toxins.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-24 08:00 AM EDT (newest of 7-day mosaic)<br/><b>Source version:</b> nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily-v3-2026-09-24<br/><b>Status:</b> LATEST AVAILABLE (daily composite)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY — auto-refresh</name>
